<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="227d" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>BFF app-only SharePoint Embedded calls target only the stamp's own container(s) — enforced in code and tests (plan G32, owner D28)</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T227 (gap G32)</phase>
    <gate>after 227b (✅); independent of 227c</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>BFF code (Sprk.Bff.Api Infrastructure/Graph + app-only SPE callers), tenant isolation (security), ArchTests; BFF §10 governance applies.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security / tenant-isolation design across many BFF call sites; judgement on which app-only calls take caller-supplied ids.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>BFF hot path; touches .claude constraints if the rule text changes (main-session-only)</parallel-reason>
    <tags>bff-api, spe, auth, tenant-isolation, model1-dedicated, testing</tags>
    <deps>227b</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make every app-only SPE call in the BFF provably target only this stamp's own container(s), and prove it with tests.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (BFF Minimal API, Microsoft Graph / SPE, ADR-007 facade, ArchTests). Load .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md and the provisioning constraint "SPE: container type per model ..." before designing.</role>

  <goal>
    An app-only SPE call (Graph client from GraphClientFactory.ForApp() — the stamp UAMI, which holds application `full` on the
    shared container type) can only reach a container the stamp owns: the configured container(s) for this environment
    (Dataverse env-var sprk_SharePointEmbeddedContainerId / EmailProcessing:DefaultContainerId / Communication:ArchiveContainerId
    — confirm the authoritative set during step 1). A request for any other container or drive is refused before Graph is called,
    and a test fails if a new app-only SPE call path bypasses the check.
  </goal>

  <justification>
    <existing>SpeFileStore facade (ADR-007) + ContainerOperations / DriveItemOperations / UploadSessionManager / SpeContainerMembershipService / IncomingCommunicationProcessor / SpeSyncOrchestrator call ForApp() for SPE; I4_SpeContainerIdLiteralTests only forbids container-id literals; ITenantContainerResolver (Diagnostics) resolves the stamp's container for H13.</existing>
    <extension>Extend the existing facade layer with one allow-list check keyed on the stamp's configured container(s); reuse ITenantContainerResolver if it is the right source. No new service unless step 1 shows the facade cannot carry it.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Owner D28: every Model 1 stamp UAMI can reach every customer's container (Microsoft: no per-container app scoping). A caller-supplied drive/container id reaching an app-only call lets one customer's request read another customer's privileged documents.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <context>
    <background>
      Researcher 2026-10-06 (.claude/agent-memory/researcher/spe-apponly-per-container-isolation-2026-10-06.md): app-only tokens
      reach all containers enabled by the container-type application permissions; container permissions apply only to delegated
      access; no per-container app scoping exists. Delegated (OBO) access is isolated by container membership. Files with
      ForApp() today (count): GraphUserService 7, IncomingCommunicationProcessor 7, SpeFileStore 7, DriveItemOperations 7,
      SpeContainerMembershipService 5, GraphSubscriptionManager 4, MailboxVerificationService 3, ContainerOperations 3, … — only
      the SPE ones matter (mail / user / subscription calls are not SPE).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/{SpeFileStore,ContainerOperations,DriveItemOperations,UploadSessionManager,GraphClientFactory}.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/SpeContainerMembershipService.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs; Services/Compose/SpeSyncOrchestrator.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Endpoints/Diagnostics/{ITenantContainerResolver,OptionsTenantContainerResolver}.cs</file>
      <file>tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/TenantIsolation/I4_SpeContainerIdLiteralTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <decisions>
    <decision date="2026-10-06" by="owner (D28)">One container type per model, one container per customer (per Dataverse environment); app-only isolation is enforced in code with tests. Do not propose a container type per customer.</decision>
  </decisions>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D28">Refuse before calling Graph; the refusal is an authorization failure (never a silent empty result).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Keep Graph inside Infrastructure/Graph; the check lives in the facade path, not scattered in endpoints.</constraint>
    <constraint source="BFF §10">Placement justification in design.md; publish-size delta vs a fresh master build; CVE check; tests for every changed Services/** file.</constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">Delegated (OBO) SPE calls are out of scope (platform-isolated). Non-SPE ForApp() calls (mail, users, subscriptions) are out of scope.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Step 1 finds an app-only SPE flow that legitimately needs a container outside the stamp's configured set (e.g. a cross-environment admin surface) → STOP and ask the owner.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Inventory every app-only SPE call path (ForApp() + SPE endpoints) and where its container/drive id comes from (config, Dataverse record, caller input). Decide the authoritative "own containers" set.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement the guard at the facade layer; route the app-only SPE paths through it.</step>
    <step order="3">Tests: unit tests for allow/deny; an ArchTest that fails if a type outside the facade calls ForApp() for SPE storage endpoints (or an equivalent structural check).</step>
    <step order="4">Docs (topology D28 note → done; constraint rule references the test); BFF §10 checks; Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A request for a container/drive outside the stamp's own set is refused before any Graph call (test), on every app-only SPE path found in step 1.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An ArchTest (or equivalent) fails when a new app-only SPE call bypasses the guard.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF unit tests, ArchTests pass; publish-size delta reported against a fresh master build; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
  </notes>
</task>
